      "status": "probable",
      "summary": "Both worker functions modify the same global non-atomic int counter. On the successful thread-creation path, main creates both workers before joining either, allowing their read-modify-write operations to overlap. writer_a holds mutex across counter += 2, while writer_b executes counter++ without synchronization. The later joins order worker completion before main continues but provide no ordering between these two worker accesses. The workers.c diff directly introduces this race by removing writer_b's mutex acquisition and release. The supplied candidate_decision.max_status limits this review to probable.",
